I want you to write a simple data legacy system with mongoose. we are versioning an entity called Resource, which has one field, a string called content.
Additionally, we have an entity called User. The user of the current session is known (it can be harcoded)
When an insert is perfomed on Resource, the id of the creating user is stored.
When an update is performed on Resource, the previous version is stored in a ResourceVersions collection. The version information contains the previous version, the operation performed and a reference to the performing user.
When a delete is performed on resource, the previous version is maintained in ResourceVersions, similar to the implementation for update.
Preferably use mongoose hooks. The user id should be made available inside the hook.
Use async/await and assume top level await is supported.